Keep the played sound queued when recording starts again after a short gap

When the sound server moves the recording to the same microphone, or restarts it for a
moment, recording stops briefly while playout goes on feeding AEC3's render queue. At the
restart (patches 0014 and 0015 mark it, patch 0010 restarts) AEC3 dropped what was queued
and found the alignment again from nothing at the next fresh played sound, and the other
side's voice leaked back for up to a second after the move.

EchoCanceller3::RestartForRecording now counts the render frames since the last recorded
frame (the render queue's size: both locks are held, and the capture side empties it at
each recorded frame). With at most 25 of them (250 ms) and a delay reported by the audio
device (SetAudioBufferDelay), it neither empties the queue nor restarts: the next recorded
frame decides. If the reported delay moved by more than 8 ms through the gap, the render
frames queued before the restart are removed and the block processor restarts as before
(RestartForRecording); otherwise it restarts keeping the played sound queued
(BlockProcessor::RestartForRecordingKeepingRender). A restart for other devices (patch
0016), more render frames or no reported delay restart as before at once.

Kept, the block processor processes the next recorded block without waiting for fresh
played sound, resets its render buffer and delay controller at it as at any restart, and
remembers the delay it had estimated before the gap. Once the render buffer has run dry
(the recorded frames delivered late, before fresh played sound) and is read again, or
after 10 blocks, it applies that delay again (AlignFromDelay). The recorded frames lost in
the gap, the render frames in it less the recorded frames delivered before fresh played
sound came, are skipped in the render buffer when it comes
(RenderDelayBuffer::SkipLostCaptureBlocks, 2.5 blocks a frame, rounded half up), short of
an underrun. The echo remover is reset at the restart's first block as with patches 0010
and 0016, transparent mode included or not as they say.

All new state of EchoCanceller3 is the capture side's, touched by the capture thread and
by the restarts, which hold both locks; the render thread only queues, as before.

Measured: not yet.

